<title>FRANCE: Bull says Q1 profit rose.</title>
<headline>Bull says Q1 profit rose.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cie des Machines Bull said on Thursday that its profits rose sharply in the first quarter, as expected.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite a difficult start to the year in Europe, the estimated net profit for the first quarter of 1997 rose sharply, as expected, due mainly to the strategic move in the personal computer business carried out at the start of April 1996,&quot; it said in its first-quarter sales statement.</p>
<p>It did not give a profit figure.</p>
<p>Bull merged its Zenith Data Systems PC division with Packard Bell NEC last April and reported a big loss for the business in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>NEC is a major shareholder in Bull, alongside Motorola and France Telecom.</p>
<p>Bull said its first-quarter 1997 sales fell 200 million francs to 4.37 billion.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
